        "procedure": "To a stirred solution of Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (0.0225 g, 0.05 mmol) and pdmH2 (0.0220 g, 0.15 mmol) in 20 mL MeOH was added solid NaO2CPh (0.0288 g, 0.2 mmol). The resulting solution was filtered after stirring for 5 h, and the filtrate was left undisturbed to concentrate slowly by evaporation. X-ray-quality white crystals of 1 formed after several days, were collected by filtration, and dried under air. Yield: 39%.",
