      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (2–300 K, 2 kG) shows χMT = 55.67 cm3 mol−1 K at 300 K, decreasing to 49.09 at 24 K and 18.13 at 2.0 K, below the 56.68 cm3 mol−1 K value for four noninteracting DyIII ions. Magnetization at 2 K reaches 26.7 Nβ at 70 kOe without saturation (expected 40 Nβ) and no hysteresis above 2.0 K. Frequency-dependent out-of-phase ac signals at zero dc field (3.5 Oe ac) indicate slow relaxation/possible SMM behavior; no χ″ peaks; similar frequency dependence under 3 kOe, so zero-field QTM is negligible above 2 K.",
